  <data key="d5">mitra</data>
</node>
<node id="Equation:eq3_likelihood">
  <data key="d0">eq3_likelihood</data>
  <data key="d1">Equation</data>
  <data key="d2">Equation (3) defines the likelihood as a product over i and x∈Ai of f_{θi}(x).</data>
  <data key="d3">mitra.pdf p.10 page_text chunk_895bf8c81d74ac37</data>
  <data key="d6">10</data>
  <data key="d4">mitra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d7">0.95</data>
  <data key="d5">mitra</data>
</node>
<node id="Equation:eq4_argmax">
  <data key="d0">eq4_argmax</data>
  <data key="d1">Equation</data>
  <data key="d2">Equation (4) defines (θ1*,…,θn*) as the argmax of L(θ1,…,θn) over Θ^n.</data>
  <data key="d3">mitra.pdf p.10 page_text chunk_895bf8c81d74ac37</data>
  <data key="d6">10</data>
  <data key="d4">mitra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d7">0.9</data>
  <data key="d5">mitra</data>
</node>
<node id="Finding:parametric_family_selection">
  <data key="d0">parametric_family_selection</data>
  <data key="d1">Finding</data>
  <data key="d2">When comparing multiple parametric families, the best fit is identified by the family yielding the highest maximized likelihood value.</data>
